  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2106.05315v1</id>
    <title>Navier-Stokes-Fourier system with Dirichlet boundary conditions</title>
    <updated>2021-06-09T18:10:55Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.05315v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.05315v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We consider the Navier--Stokes--Fourier system describing the motion of a compressible, viscous, and heat conducting fluid in a bounded domain with general non-homogeneous Dirichlet boundary conditions for the velocity and the absolute temperature, with the associated boundary conditions for the density on the inflow part. We introduce a new concept of weak solution based on the satisfaction of the entropy inequality together with a balance law for the ballistic energy. We show the weak-strong uniqueness principle as well as the existence of global-in-time solutions.</summary>
    <category term="math.AP" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2021-06-09T18:10:55Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.AP"/>
    <author>
      <name>Nilasis Chaudhuri</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Eduard Feireisl</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2207.00991v1</id>
    <title>On weak(measure valued)-strong uniqueness for Navier-Stokes-Fourier system with Dirichlet boundary condition</title>
    <updated>2022-07-03T09:25:02Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.00991v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.00991v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper, our goal is to define a measure valued solution of compressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system for a heat conducting fluid with Dirichlet boundary condition for temperature in a bounded domain. The definition is based on the weak formulation of entropy inequality and ballistic energy inequality. Moreover, we obtain the weak(measure valued)-strong uniqueness property of this solution with the help of relative energy.</summary>
    <category term="math.AP" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2022-07-03T09:25:02Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.AP"/>
    <author>
      <name>Nilasis Chaudhuri</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1812.01403v3</id>
    <title>Ballistic random walks in random environment as rough paths: convergence and area anomaly</title>
    <updated>2020-08-07T08:20:19Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.01403v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1812.01403v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Annealed functional CLT in the rough path topology is proved for the standard class of ballistic random walks in random environment. Moreover, the `area anomaly', i.e. a deterministic linear correction for the second level iterated integral of the rescaled path, is identified in terms of a stochastic area on a regeneration interval. The main theorem is formulated in more general settings, namely for any discrete process with uniformly bounded increments which admits a regeneration structure where the regeneration times have finite moments. Here the largest finite moment translates into the degree of regularity of the rough path topology. In particular, the convergence holds in the $α$-Hölder rough path topology for all $α&lt;1/2$ whenever all moments are finite, which is the case for the class of ballistic random walks in random environment. The latter may be compared to a special class of random walks in Dirichlet environments for which the regularity $α&lt;1/2$ is bounded away from $1/2$, explicitly in terms of the corresponding trap parameter.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2018-12-04T13:32:55Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>15 pages, 2 figures</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.PR"/>
    <author>
      <name>Olga Lopusanschi</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Tal Orenshtein</name>
    </author>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.1333v1</id>
    <title>Stable fluctuations for ballistic random walks in random environment on Z</title>
    <updated>2010-04-08T13:38:11Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.1333v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1004.1333v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We consider transient random walks in random environment on Z in the positive speed (ballistic) and critical zero speed regimes. A classical result of Kesten, Kozlov and Spitzer proves that the hitting time of level $n$, after proper centering and normalization, converges to a completely asymmetric stable distribution, but does not describe its scale parameter. Following a previous article by three of the authors, where the (non-critical) zero speed case was dealt with, we give a new proof of this result in the subdiffusive case that provides a complete description of the limit law. The case of Dirichlet environment turns out to be remarkably explicit.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2010-04-08T13:38:11Z</published>
