  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.20758v1</id>
    <title>Convergence of a finite volume method to weak solutions for the compressible Navier-Stokes-Fourier system</title>
    <updated>2026-03-21T11:13:41Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.20758v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.20758v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We prove strong convergence of an upwind-type finite volume method to a weak solution of the Navier-Stokes-Fourier system with the Dirichlet boundary conditions. The limit solution satisfies a weak form of the mass and momentum equations, together with a weak form of the entropy and ballistic energy inequalities, and complies with the weak-strong uniqueness principle. The finite volume method uses piecewise-constant spatial approximations. The convergence proof is based on a combination of delicate consistency estimates with a careful analysis of the oscillations of numerical densities via renormalisation of the continuity equation.</summary>
    <category term="math.NA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-03-21T11:13:41Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>44 pages</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.NA"/>
    <author>
      <name>Eduard Feireisl</name>
    </author>
    <author>
