    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1409.5528v1</id>
    <title>A Quenched Functional Central Limit Theorem for Random Walks in Random Environments under $(T)_γ$</title>
    <updated>2014-09-19T06:20:31Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.5528v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.5528v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We prove a quenched central limit theorem for random walks in i.i.d. weakly elliptic random environments in the ballistic regime. Such theorems have been proved recently by Rassoul-Agha and Seppäläinen in [10] and Berger and Zeitouni in [2] under the assumption of large finite moments for the regeneration time. In this paper, with the extra $(T)_γ$ condition of Sznitman we reduce the moment condition to ${\Bbb E}(τ^2(\ln τ)^{1+m})&lt;+\infty$ for $m&gt;1+1/γ$, which allows the inclusion of new non-uniformly elliptic examples such as Dirichlet random environments.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2014-09-19T06:20:31Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>17 p</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.PR"/>
